# Proof: F-V3-ENGINE
# Top: v3_engine
# Assumptions: Initial sampled reset; fetch_data and fetch_written are free
#   every cycle, so every instruction stream is over-approximated. Pin levels,
#   queue levels/data and the CRC value are free inputs too.
# Properties: Return-stack depth bound, commits only strobe owned pins, the
#   external queue levels are never over/underflowed, a bubble cycle has no
#   side effects, errors are sticky, a taken branch costs exactly two cycles,
#   RET on an empty stack faults and halts, and each commit, queue, CRC and
#   clear-missed strobe equals its op retiring.
# Method: temporal induction.
# Scope and abstractions: formal/README.md.

read_verilog -formal -DFORMAL -I src src/v3_engine.v
prep -top v3_engine
flatten
memory_map
opt
async2sync
dffunmap
sat -seq 4 -tempinduct -maxsteps 16 -set-assumes -prove-asserts -verify
